  "result": "If I could change the world in one way, I\u2019d seed every human heart with genuine, effortless empathy\u2014the ability to feel another person\u2019s joys and pains as if they were your own.  \n\nWhy empathy?  \n\u2022 It underpins every positive change: when we truly understand others\u2019 struggles, we\u2019re motivated to alleviate suffering\u2014driving down poverty, hunger, and inequality.  \n\u2022 It heals divisions: whether between cultures, races or nations, empathy dissolves \u201cus vs. them\u201d thinking and makes cooperation the default.  \n\u2022 It protects our planet: feeling the impact of environmental degradation on future generations or distant communities fuels collective action on climate change.  \n\u2022 It nurtures mental health: knowing you\u2019re seen and understood eases isolation, anxiety and despair.  \n\nWith universal empathy as our baseline, violence and prejudice would shrink, public policies would center human dignity and environmental stewardship, and societies would invest in education, health care and sustainable living\u2014not out of abstract duty, but out of heartfelt concern for one another.  \n\nIn short, empathy doesn\u2019t just make us kinder individuals\u2014it transforms institutions, economies and ecosystems. Plant that single seed, and a more just, peaceful and flourishing world would grow.",
